**Understanding the metrics**

- **Compliance Score**: Percentage of compliant rule-resource combinations in this conformance pack. This is calculated as the number of compliant rule-resource pairs divided by the total number of rule-resource pairs evaluated.
- **Failed Controls**: Number of config rules that have failed compliance.

> <span style="display: inline-block; width: 16px; height: 16px; background-color: #60a5fa; border-radius: 50%; text-align: center; line-height: 16px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: bold; color: white; margin-right: 4px;">i</span>**Note**: A single config rule may generate multiple findings across different resources. For example, one EC2 rule may produce findings for each non-compliant instance in your account. The compliance score reflects compliance at the rule-resource level, not just per rule.